Unreleased
---
Cleanup
- The scroll offset of a ribbon page is clamped in one place. The legal range
  was written down four times - a pair of hand-rolled if-chains in the wheel
  path, a qBound() in the button path, and twice more in the layout pass - which
  agreed only because someone had read them against each other. They now all
  fold into RibbonPagePrivate::clampXBase(), so a path that moves the content
  cannot answer "how far" differently from its neighbours. No behaviour change.
  tst_RibbonPage::wheelAndButtonsShareOneRange drives both paths to both ends
  and compares them pixel for pixel, which is the check the duplication made
  impossible to write before.
- RibbonGalleryGroupItemDelegate loses the two paint helpers that held nothing.
  paintIconWithText() and paintIconWithTextWordWrap() were one line each, and that
  line was the call to QStyledItemDelegate::paint() the surrounding switch reaches
  for anyway; the two text presentations now make that call directly, and only
  paintIconOnly() - the one presentation that paints something the base does not -
  keeps a helper of its own. The delegate is private to the library, so no caller
  outside it could have overridden the pair. No behaviour change.
- RibbonButton::actionEvent() is gone, an override whose entire body was the call
  to QToolButton::actionEvent(). The base implementation is reached directly now.
  A subclass that overrides actionEvent() keeps working: the slot it overrides is
  QWidget's, not the removed one's. No behaviour change.
- The HELP_DRAW_RECT macro in ribbongroup.cpp was defined unconditionally while
  its two call sites sit inside #ifdef QX_RIBBON_DEBUG_HELP_DRAW, so every ordinary
  build carried a macro it never expanded. The definition now sits under the same
  guard as the one in ribbonbutton.cpp, which keeps the opt-in layout aid intact
  and the two files consistent.
- RibbonActionsManagerModelPrivate::m_seatchText is spelled m_searchText. The
  member records the text the model is filtered by; the class is private to its
  cpp, so the rename reaches nothing outside it.

Feature
- RibbonBar::resizeRibbonNow() does the layout resizeRibbon() asks for before it
  returns, instead of on the next event loop pass. resizeRibbon() defers for a
  reason (see doc/pages/limitations.md, "RibbonBar resize is deferred") and the
  deferral is observable: the caller has already changed something the user is
  looking at, and the previous geometry stays on screen for that pass. The two
  callers inside this class that needed it now - setMinimized() and
  showMinimumButton() - built the event themselves; that idiom now has a name, and
  RibbonMainWindow forwards it for callers that hold the window rather than the
  bar. tst_RibbonAppWindow::flagsChangeLaysTheGroupsOutImmediately
- KeyTips: pressing Alt labels the application button and the visible pages with
  letter badges; picking a page's letter switches to it and descends one level to
  label that page's buttons - a button's mnemonic where it has one, a generated
  A-Z letter otherwise. A control runs on click, Esc or Alt leaves the mode, and a
  resize puts the badges away. RibbonGallery is a KeyTip target too: its letter
  moves focus into the gallery, which then takes over the keyboard.
- RibbonButton shows a rich ScreenTip on hover: the action's text without its
  mnemonic, its statusTip, and its shortcut, in a shared frameless tool window
  that follows the pointer. An action with neither a statusTip nor a shortcut
  keeps the plain tooltip.
- Add the LightFluent2016Theme and LightFluent2019Theme ribbon themes. They reuse
  the Office 2013 selectors with the palette remapped to the Fluent accent and
  neutral colours (2019 the lighter chrome). The two enumerators are appended
  after CustomTheme so the existing theme values do not shift, because
  RibbonMainWindow exposes the theme as an int.
- RibbonQuickAccessBar: the customize menu now ends with the Office-style
  "Customize Quick Access Toolbar..." entry, after a separator, which emits the
  new customizeDialogRequested() signal for the host to open its dialog. The entry
  action is owned by the bar rather than the menu, because the menu clears itself
  when it hides and would delete an action it owned.
- RibbonGallery is keyboard reachable: it takes focus and handles the arrow keys
  (moving the current item, clamped at the ends), Enter/Space (activating the
  current item) and PageUp/PageDown (the two scroll buttons).
- RibbonBar: right-clicking opens a context menu with "Minimize the Ribbon"
  (checkable, tracking isMinimized()) and the quick access bar's customize entry.
  Subclasses can extend it by overriding addContextMenuActions().
- RibbonPage and RibbonGroup mirror their title into accessibleName (mnemonics
  stripped, kept in step with windowTitleChanged) and the ribbon bar carries a
  stable name; a QAccessible factory gives the painted page and group containers
  the Pane and Grouping roles, which their custom painting otherwise hid from
  assistive tools.
- A page that runs out of room narrows its groups before it falls back to its
  scroll buttons. A group has a reduced presentation in which a button that would
  own a whole column is packed as a small one instead, trading rows for width; the
  page reduces groups from the right until they fit, so a page with room always
  shows every group at full width, and the left and right scroll buttons appear
  only when the narrowest form of every group still overflows.
- RibbonMdiArea is a tabbed-document MDI area that keeps the ribbon in step
  with the active document. Documents open as tabs by default (tabbed view
  plus document mode, closable and movable), and a document may carry a
  RibbonPage that is shown while the document is active and hidden while it
  is not, so switching tabs swaps the ribbon pages - the treatment a ribbon
  application gives its documents. Of the pages it manages, only the active
  document's stays up, and none at all while nothing is active; a document
  added without a page leaves the ribbon alone, and so does a page that is on
  no RibbonBar. The area paints nothing of its own - the document tabs are the
  plain tab bar QMdiArea drives - so it adds no visual semantics a theme would
  have to follow. tst_RibbonMdiArea drives the swap, the close paths and the
  guards on both legs.

- RibbonBackstageView: add the full-takeover backstage panel the application button
  opens - Office's File menu as a panel that covers the ribbon bar's host and lays
  the document commands down a left column and their pages to the right of it.
  addAction()/addSeparator()/addPage() fill the column; setActivePage()/activePage()
  swap the right-hand page; open() shows the panel and Esc or the styled close
  button hides it, unless setClosePrevented() holds it open; the panel answers
  RibbonBar::applicationButtonClicked by itself, so a host that wants it to do
  something else disconnects that signal. The column, its button and its separator
  carry the qx_RibbonBackstage* object names, so a theme styles them the way it
  styles the rest of the ribbon, and the panel paints nothing of its own - the
  column hugs the left edge and the page fills what is left. tst_RibbonBackstageView
  drives open/close, the page swap, the host-resize follow and the application-button
  toggle; Example_Ribbon_Backstage is a host that ends in the backstage.

- RibbonStatusBar: add the ribbon-styled status bar (QStatusBar). A host puts
  plain-text segments on the left and view switches on the right the way Office's
  ribbon status bar does. addAction() adds a left segment the host updates by
  setting the action's text, addSeparator() adds a hairline between two of them,
  and addPermanentAction() adds a right-hand switch that stays put while
  showMessage() scrolls its text across the left. The bar carries the
  qx_RibbonStatusBar object name and paints nothing of its own, so a dark theme
  styles it the way it styles the rest of the ribbon - the dark themes already
  carry a QStatusBar rule; the segments and the permanent buttons carry their own
  qx_RibbonStatusBar* names. tst_RibbonStatusBar drives the two sections, the text
  tracking and the showMessage() hide; Example_Ribbon_StatusBar is a host with
  both sections filled.

- RibbonSliderPane: add the Office zoom control - a minus button, a slider track
  and a plus button in one compact pane, the control a ribbon application puts at
  the right end of its status bar. The buttons step by singleStep (auto-repeat on
  hold), the track reports valueChanged() when the level settles and sliderMoved()
  for every step of a drag; setRange() bounds both and setScrollButtons(false)
  keeps the track alone. It is a plain widget, so a host joins it to the permanent
  section with QStatusBar::addPermanentWidget() and a message never pushes it out.
  Nothing paints here either: the stock widgets carry the qx_RibbonSliderPane*
  object names and the buttons draw their glyphs from the palette, so they read on
  a dark theme without one carrying icons. tst_RibbonSliderPane drives the range,
  the buttons and the forwarding of both signals.

Interface
- RibbonMdiArea: add RibbonMdiArea
- RibbonBackstageView: add RibbonBackstageView (QWidget)
- RibbonStatusBar: add RibbonStatusBar (QStatusBar)
- RibbonSliderPane: add RibbonSliderPane (QWidget)
- RibbonQuickAccessBar: add customizeDialogRequested and actionCustomizeDialog
- RibbonGalleryGroup: add triggerCurrentItem
- RibbonBar: add overridable addContextMenuActions
- RibbonGroup: add setReduced and isReduced

Bugfix
- The KeyTip letter pool was filled with QList<QString>(int), a constructor only
  Qt 6 has, so the ribbon did not compile against Qt 5. The list is resized
  instead, which both versions provide.

0.12.2
---
Cleanup
- Drop the Qt 5.7 branches in RibbonGridContainerPrivate::init() and
  RibbonCustomizeWidget::initConnection(). Both guarded the QOverload spelling
  of the connect() calls against the static_cast spelling, and the threshold is
  below the 5.15 minimum, so the QOverload form is now used unconditionally.

Bugfix
- RibbonPage scrolled to the right end and then widened left a gap as wide as
  the resize between the last group and the right edge, with the scroll buttons
  still reporting the right end as reached. The page clamps its horizontal
  offset only when the content stops overflowing, so an offset that was legal
  for the narrower page stayed behind the raised lower bound of its legal range
  and the content stopped short of the viewport. The offset is now clamped
  against the width the layout has just measured - the size hint total carries
  the contents margins and none of the expanding width, so clamping with that
  would land on the wrong pixel - and the geometry of the same pass is shifted
  by the amount the offset moved instead of being measured twice. Clicking a
  scroll button healed the gap before, which made it a transient visual defect
  rather than corrupted state.
- The window button group came up in the top-left corner, over the tab bar,
  and only moved to the top-right after the window was resized by hand. The
  ribbon lays itself out through resizeRibbon(), which queues a resize event,
  and a window is normally still hidden when that event is delivered: the
  AppShell demo drains the queue through QxSplashScreen::step() while the
  window is being built. Every layout decision in the four resize and
  minimumWidth functions asked isVisible(), which is false for the whole
  window at that point, so the group was skipped and left at its default
  position, and nothing re-ran the layout until the window happened to be
  resized. Those functions now ask whether a widget is explicitly hidden,
  through one helper, so the first layout - the one that runs while the
  window is hidden - produces the geometry the first painted frame shows.
  The paint functions keep isVisible(): they only run while the window is
  visible and they ask the other question.
- WindowButtonGroupPrivate::sizeHint() was the second half of the same
  defect: it summed the button widths from isVisible(), so a group sized
  while the window was hidden came out zero wide. Fixing the ribbon alone
  would therefore have placed a zero-width group on the title bar with its
  buttons stacked on top of each other. The size hint now reads the hidden
  flag as well.

0.12.1
---
Bugfix
- RibbonCustomizeWidget recorded a "move down" on an action as a "move up": the
  action branch handed -1 to makeChangeActionOrderCustomizeData(), and on that
  function -1 means up while 1 means down - which is what the page and group
  branches pass. apply() moves the action to idx + indexValue, so the recorded
  change moved it the wrong way.
- The ribbon bar named its tab bar twice, so the second name clobbered the first:
  the tab bar ended up called "qx_RibbonStackedWidget" and the stacked widget had
  no name at all. The stacked widget now carries that name and the tab bar keeps
  "qx_RibbonTabBar". No shipped stylesheet refers to either name today, so nothing
  visible changes - but the names are part of what a caller can target from its
  own stylesheet, and the bar was answering wrongly for both.
- RibbonPage left two of its private fields uninitialised. RibbonPagePrivate's
  constructor set the page's cached content width and its horizontal scroll
  offset nowhere, so a wheel event or a scroll button click that arrived before
  the first layout pass compared and clamped an indeterminate value. Both now
  start at 0 - the value the first layout pass gives a page with no content.

Cleanup
- RibbonCustomizeWidget no longer declares isChanged() and model(). Nothing in
  the tree called either one. The class is not exported, and the limitations page
  records the dialog that hosts it as the whole interface, so both accessors were
  answering for state the class keeps to itself: the ribbon tree view and the
  item look-ups already reach the model directly.
- Six places posted the deferred resize by hand - a line-for-line copy of what
  RibbonBar::resizeRibbon() already does - so the reason the resize is queued
  rather than run in place was written down in one place and repeated in six.
  They all call resizeRibbon() now, which makes it the single entry point for
  "the ribbon changed shape, ask for a resize". No behaviour change: the posted
  event is identical.

0.12.0
---
Bugfix
- RibbonTheme::setTheme(RibbonTheme::CustomTheme) dereferenced the widget pointer
  it was handed, which made the documented way of calling it - the widget argument
  defaults to nullptr - a crash on a null pointer. CustomTheme now clears the
  application stylesheet when there is no widget, which is what loadTheme() has
  always done for a nullptr (A7)
- RibbonCtrlContainer built with Qt::Vertical centred its icon while one switched
  to Qt::Vertical afterwards left-aligned it: init() set the alignment without
  looking at the orientation, and only setOrientation() applied the rule. Both
  paths now start from the same one (A7)

Interface
- FramelessHelper and RibbonWindow are removed (deprecated in 4.2, K27 / K26).
  FramelessHelper was the frameless backend RibbonWindow carried so that qxribbon
  needs no dependency on qxwindow: Qt::FramelessWindowHint plus simulated hit
  testing, move and resize, with a native path on Windows under Qt 5. Its Qt 6
  path - and, outside Windows, every path - is the incomplete half, where a window
  shown maximised for the first time cannot be restored; see the limitations page.
  RibbonWindow is RibbonMainWindow plus that backend and nothing else, so the two
  went together rather than leaving an empty shell behind. On every Qt version the
  answer is QxApp::RibbonAppWindow, which frames the same RibbonMainWindow through
  qxwindow; on Qt 5 that costs a dependency on qxapp, and qxwindow's native
  backend does build there. Every sample moves to RibbonMainWindow. See
  doc/pages/migration.md, section "4.3 已删除"

Interface
- RibbonGalleryViewport loses QX_RIBBON_EXPORT. It lives in ribbongallery_p.h and
  was privatized on purpose; only the export macro still claimed otherwise. Every
  .h in a library's SOURCES is installed, private ones included, so the header
  was reachable on disk without the class ever being public API - a caller that
  wants its own gallery popup overrides RibbonGallery::showMoreTrigger() and
  never names this class. It is the only exported class in a _p.h in the tree

Cleanup
- Remove the Qt version branch below 5.15 in FramelessWidgetDataNativeWin::devicePixelRatio,
  which K1 set as the minimum; QWidget::screen() has been the way to reach the
  screen since then

Bugfix
- QX_RIBBON_DEPRECATED_SINCE(major, minor) never answered true for a deprecation
  that had already happened: QX_RIBBON_DISABLE_DEPRECATED_BEFORE defaulted to
  QX_RIBBON_VERSION, so the deprecation point was compared against the version
  being built - (0,11,0) > (0,11,0) is false - and the answer flipped back to
  false on every minor bump. The default is now a fixed floor, so an API stays
  declared for as long as it is inside its removal buffer (K26), and raising the
  cutoff is what compiles it out. tst_qxdeprecated covers all seven libraries

0.11.0
---
Deprecated
- FramelessHelper: it is the frameless backend of RibbonWindow, and on Windows
  with Qt 5 it is the working path; everywhere else - including every Qt 6
  platform - the path it implements is the incomplete half, where a window
  shown maximised for the first time cannot be restored. It is marked with
  QT_DEPRECATED_X and points at QxApp::RibbonAppWindow, which goes through
  qxwindow. RibbonWindow itself is unchanged and still uses it. Removal needs
  at least one release of warning first (K26).

Added
- RibbonStyleOption: add setBaseHeight(), setTitleBarHeight() and setTabBarHeight()
  so the ribbon size layout can be tuned without subclassing; recalc() keeps an
  explicit title/tab and only recomputes the four derived ribbon-bar heights

Cleanup
- RibbonButton: drop the stale "todo" in the FontChange handler - it asked for
  exactly what the next three lines already do, and sizeHint() recomputes its
  cached value on every call
- RibbonStyleOption: drop the "@todo define the ribbon layout in a config file";
  the extension point it described already exists - the class is virtual and
  RibbonFactory::setRibbonStyleOption() takes a subclass - and a config file is a
  caller-side policy rather than a gap here

0.10.2
---
Bugfix
- RibbonMainWindow: keep the window at least as wide as the ribbon bar needs
- RibbonGridContainer: make enterEvent an override on Qt 6, where its parameter
  is QEnterEvent *; the Qt 5 signature hid the virtual there and the handler
  never ran, which left a menu with two entries looking current

